  "id": "voice/input-levels-fire-at-most-ten-a-second-per-session",
  "title": "Frames a session sends over one second fire at most ten input levels, 100 ms apart, each session its own",
  "rules": [
    "§12.5",
    "§9.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-12.5-030"
  ],
  "requires_features": [
    "voice"
  ],
  "notes": "Each of two sessions sends a frame every 21 ms of the virtual clock, 48 frames in 987 ms: unthrottled, 48 levels each. The 100 ms interval falls between two frames (105 ms, then 84 ms), never on one, where two clock readings would be compared to the edge: levels at 0, 105, 210 ... 945 ms, ten per session, whatever the other session sent.",
